  "raw_text": "103\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb45\n):\n \nBaha kiamka 10 nani ba Israel kingka lâka nina mâkan\n \n–\n \nThose 10 tribes were named the kingdom of Israel\n \n/ Esas 10\n\ntribus fueron nombradas el reino de Israel\n)\n\nUpla almuk kiamka\n \n–\n \ngenealogy, ancestry\n \n/ genealogía, ascendencia\n\nKiamp\n \n(\ndb,dict,dictu,lfb\n;\n \nKyamp\n-\nlv,my\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncamp\n \n/ campamento\n\nKianan\n \n(\ndictu,dict\n;\n \nKanyun\n-\nmy\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncannon\n \n/ cañón\n\nKiandil\n \n(\ndb,dict,dictu,my,mwb\n;\n \nKyandil-\nbh\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncandle\n \n/ vela\n\nKiandil mina\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncandle stand, lampstand\n \n/ candelabro\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\ndb-Param Marikan 1:20; mwb-11/19\n):\n \nKiandil mina gul ni paskan 7 ba\n \n–\n \nThe 7 lampstands made with gold\n \n/ Los 7\ncandelabros de oro)\n\nKiansa sikniska\n \n(\nlv,fy,gf\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncancer\n \n/ cáncer\n\nKiapital\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nKapital\n\nKiaptin\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncaptain, boss\n \n/ capitán, jefe\n\nKiasma\n \n(a/t:\n \nKyasma\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nsmoke, fumes\n \n/ humo, humos\n\nKiasma kîa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsmell of smoke\n \n/ olor a humo\n\nKiasma daukaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nKiasma dingkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto smoke\n \n/\n \nfumar\n\nKiasma dingkaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nKiasma daukaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto smoke, to be smoking\n \n/ fumar\n\nKiasma dadaukra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nsmoker, person who smokes\n \n/ fumador, persona que fuma\n\nKiastanit\n \n(a/t:\n \nKiastinit\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nnet that is thrown to catch fish, shrimp and turtle\n \n/ red que se lanza para pescar y para\natrapar camarones y tortugas\n\nKiastanit miskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto use a net (kiastanit) to catch fish, shrimp, and turtle\n \n/ usar un red (kiastanit) para pescar\ny atrapar camarones y tortugas\n\nKiauaia\n \n(\ndict,dictu\n; not in / no en:\n \ndb,publicaciones\n)\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nKiaubaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto come to be gathered together, to\ncome to be piled up together\n \n/ venir a estar juntos, venir a estar amontonados juntos\n\nKiaubaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKiubaia\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nKiauaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto\n \ngat\nher, to pile up, to collect, to rake, to gather together\n \n/\n \nrecoger,\namontonar, colectar, rastrillar, juntar\n\nKiaubi alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto embrace, to hug\n \n/ abrazar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKlubi alkaia\n)\n\nKiaubi wilkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto pick up and tie or bind, to collect and tie or bind\n \n/ recoger y amarrar, colectar y amarrar\n\nKiawalaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKyawalaia\n,\n \nKia walaia\n,\n \nKîa walaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto kiss, to smell\n \n/ besar, oler\n\nKiawalanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nKyawalanka\n-\nmy51\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nkiss, kissing\n \n/ beso, besos\n\nKikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto laugh, to smile\n \n/ reír, sonreír\n\nKupia ra kikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto laugh to yourself, to laugh in your heart\n \n/ reírte a de ti mismo, reírse por dentro, reír en tu\ncorazón\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb-9\n):\n \nSara ai kupia ra kikan bara lukan: “¿Rait pali luhpa kum brimna almuk takri na ra?”\n \n–\n \nSarah laughed in her\n\nheart and thought “Could I really have a child at this old age?”\n \n/ Sara se rió en su corazón y pensó: \"¿Realmente podría\ntener un hijo a esta edad?\")\n\nLawaska kikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto taunt, to mock, to deride, to ridicule\n \n/ burlarse, ridiculizar\n\n(Construct:\n \nLaiwaska kikaia\n;\n \nLamwaska kikaia\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Jirimaya 10:15\n):\n \nlawaska kikaia dukia\n \n–\n \nthing to be mocked\n \n/ cosa para ser burlado)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Jirimaya 20:7\n):\n \nupla sut yang laiwaska kikisa\n \n–\n \neveryone ridicules me\n \n/ todos me ridiculizan)\n\nLawaska kiki aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak with taunts, to speak with mocking, to speak with ridicule, to speak\nsarcastically\n \n/ hablar con burlas, hablar con ridículo, hablar sarcásticamente\n\nKilumita\n \n(\njl\n,bm,km,\nfy\n;\n \nKilamitra\n-\nbh\n,lv,\nmy\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nkilometer\n \n/ kilómetro\n\nKîn\n \n(n/s) (a/t:\n \nKiin\n-\ndict,dictu\n)\n \n–\n \ncane, staff, walking stick\n \n/ bastón, bordón\n\n(Construct:\n \nKînki, Kînkam, Kînka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb18\n):\n \nKînka ba piuta kum takan!\n \n–\n \nThe stick became a snake!\n \n/ ¡El palo se convirtió en una serpiente!)\n\nKing\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nking\n \n/ rey\n\nBan kaia Kingka\n \n–\n \nKing of Eternity\n \n(\n1 Timothy 1:17\n) / Rey de la eternidad (1 Timoteo 1:17)\n\nKing aimakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rule, to reign\n \n/ gobernar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nRul munaia\n)\n\nKing aimakaia raitka\n \n–\n \nright to rule, sovereignty\n \n/ derecho a gobernar, soberanía\n\nGâd king aimakaia raitka\n \n–\n \nGod’s\n \nright to rule,\n \nGod’s\n \nsovereignty\n \n/ derecho de Dios a gobernar,\nsoberanía de Dios\n\nKing iwaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthrone\n \n/ trono",
